<header><p class="st-kicker">princely state · Indian princely states</p><h1 class="st-title">Gondal State</h1><p class="st-meta">1634 CE – 1948 CE · capital Gondal</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Jadeja Rajput state of Kathiawar made famous by Maharaja Bhagvatsinhji, a reformer who abolished taxes and made girls' schooling compulsory.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Gondal was founded in 1634 by Kumbhoji I, a member of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jadeja">Jadeja</a> house of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/rajkot-state">Rajkot</a>, who received the area as his share. His successor Kumbhoji II expanded the state in the 18th century.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Thakore Sahibs ruled a prosperous <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cotton">cotton</a>-growing territory. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharaja">Maharaja</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bhagvatsinhji">Bhagvatsinhji</a>, who reigned from 1888 to 1944 and trained as a doctor at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edinburgh">Edinburgh</a>, built railways and schools, made education compulsory for girls, abolished many taxes and sponsored the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bhagavadgomandal">Bhagavadgomandal</a> Gujarati encyclopedia. It was an eleven-gun salute state.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Gondal merged into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/saurashtra-state">United State of Saurashtra</a> in 1948 and became part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gujarat">Gujarat</a> in 1960. The town retains its palaces and a reputation as a model state.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/gondal-state.jpg" alt="Gondal State" width="320" height="325"><figcaption>Image: Dr. Andreas Birken at German Wikipedia · CC BY-SA 3.0 de · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:SaurashtraKart.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1634 CE – 1948 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>princely state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Gondal</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Kumbhoji I, Bhagvatsinhji</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Gujarati</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Gondal</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1791&amp;focus=gondal-state" aria-label="Gondal State on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6578 1366 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Gondal State lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6898 1622L7364 1601M6898 1622L7364 1602M6898 1622L6896 1610"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7364 1601h0M7364 1602h0M6896 1610h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6898 1622h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6898 1622h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Gondal. <a href="/atlas?year=1791&amp;focus=gondal-state">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
